## Follow-up Questions

- How would you differentiate bottlenecks between DB writes and external risk-service calls?
- What metrics would you automate alerting on, and how would you adjust tests if latency targets drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a realistic real-time WebSocket scenario and beginner-friendly granularity (handshake, message latency, backpressure) that is frequently encountered in consumer apps and fintech-grade feeds.

## Key Concepts
- WebSocket handshake latency and maintenance cost
- Latency vs throughput trade-offs
- Backpressure signals and broker queues
- Ramp-up strategy and warm-up
- Basic observability: latency percentiles, error rate

## Code Example
